{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/zd8byn","slideIndex":2,"text":"The professional identity I’m building is also shaped by how I want to work. Security matters to me because software often handles information people expect to be protected. I want to keep learning how to design systems with appropriate access and careful data handling.\n\nResponsibility means considering the people affected by technology, not only whether a system works. My interest in responsible technology has also led me to explore questions of ethics and governance around predictive AI in healthcare. Continuous learning is essential in a field that changes quickly, so I aim to keep strengthening my fundamentals as I learn new tools.\n\nThese values help define the professional brand I want to present: technically curious, careful with responsibility, and focused on building useful systems people can trust.\n\nSource: https://lk.linkedin.com/in/charithkalhara"}
